# W44-104 — admit-DCT64-on-terminal-class A/B HONEST STOP (2026-05-20)
#
# Status: [RULED OUT — W44-103 candidate A hypothesis falsified]
#
# Workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-104-dct64-search-screen (jj sibling on main)
# Parent: f2682707 (W44-103 terminal SSIM2 attribution dump)
# Harness: jxl-encoder/examples/w44_104_dct64_screen_ab.rs
# Bench wall: ~50 min for 23 of 52 cells (terminal subset; killed early once result was
# decisive). Each cell = 2 trials × 2 modes (baseline / admit) + 2 metric decodes.
# Threads: 1.
#
# Modes:
#   - baseline: default (W44-65/W44-68 auto-fires on terminal-class: try_dct64=false
#     AND try_dct32=false when median(mask1x1) >= 99.5).
#   - admit   : `LossyConfig::with_dct_suppress_hint(Some(false))` — bypass the
#     auto-suppression. At e>=7, this admits the full DCT64-class search
#     (DCT64X64, DCT64X32, DCT32X64). At e>=5, this also re-admits the
#     DCT32-class search (DCT32X32, DCT32X16, DCT16X32).
#
# Background — what W44-103 found:
# ───────────────────────────────
# terminal.png d=4 is the largest SSIM2 inferiority cluster vs cjxl (-4.6 to
# -5.6 across all 5 efforts). The W44-103 dump
# (benchmarks/w44_103_terminal_ssim2_dump_2026-05-19.tsv) attributed this to
# three concurrent root causes:
#
#   1. DCT16X16 over-firing 25× at ALL efforts (4870 vs cjxl 287).
#   2. DCT64 family ENTIRELY absent from our output (0 vs cjxl 369 first-blocks).
#   3. e8/e9 buttloop convergence on qac 13-17× LOWER than cjxl.
#
# W44-103 candidate A (highest expected EV per analysis): close the DCT64
# selection gap. Hypothesis: "cjxl picks ~370 DCT64 first-blocks per cell on
# the blank screen-background bottom-row regions. Why does our DCT64 search
# never win? Likely entropy_mul64=2.25 too high OR find_best_64x64_transform
# exits early OR mask1x1 quant bias."
#
# Root cause traced (this chunk, hour 1):
# ──────────────────────────────────────
# The DCT64 search NEVER RUNS on terminal — it is *gated out before evaluation*
# by the W44-65/W44-68 default-on auto suppression in `vardct/encoder.rs:2872-2976`:
#
#   let w44_65_suppress_dct64 = match self.dct_suppress_hint {
#       Some(b) => b,
#       None => mask1x1_median.is_some_and(|med| med >= 99.5),
#   };
#   if w44_65_suppress_dct64 {
#       p.try_dct64 = false;  // W44-65
#       p.try_dct32 = false;  // W44-68
#   }
#
# terminal.png saturates at mask1x1 median ≈ 100, so both flips fire — the
# AC strategy search never even calls `find_best_64x64_transform`. This is
# NOT a bug in the search itself; it is a deliberate gate.
#
# Smoke test (cell 1, terminal e7 d=4):
#   hint=None         => 31164 bytes (auto suppression fires)
#   hint=Some(true)   => 31164 bytes (force suppress; identical)
#   hint=Some(false)  => 32443 bytes (admit; +4.10% bytes)
#
# The hint plumbing works. The next question: does admitting move SSIM2?
#
# Measurement (23 terminal cells × 5 efforts × 5 distances):
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Effort × distance grid (admit minus baseline; positive ssim2_delta = quality improved):
#
# | effort | d=2          | d=3          | d=4          | d=5           | d=6          |
# |--------|--------------|--------------|--------------|---------------|--------------|
# | e5     | +0.21 / +0.8 | +1.04 / +0.9 | +0.24 / -0.1 | +0.16 / +0.4  | +0.29 / +0.9 |
# | e6     | +0.43 / +0.9 | +1.04 / -0.8 | +0.26 / +1.5 | +0.23 / +0.7  | +0.40 / +1.5 |
# | e7     | -0.10 / +2.4 | +0.79 / +1.0 | +0.03 / +4.1 | -0.28 / +3.5  | +0.53 / +4.0 |
# | e8     | +1.02 / +3.8 | +0.75 / +3.7 | -1.10 / +4.6 | -1.51 / +5.7  | -0.21 / +3.5 |
# | e9     | +1.02 / +3.7 | +0.75 / +3.3 | -1.10 / +4.3 | (incomplete)  | (incomplete) |
#
# (cell value = `ssim2_delta_abs` / `bytes_delta_pct`; e5/e6 are pre-DCT64
# effort gate, so admit only re-enables DCT32-class; e7+ admits the full
# DCT64-class search)
#
# Acceptance gate from task spec:
# ───────────────────────────────
#   "≥3 SSIM2 points improvement on at least 3 of the 5 terminal d=4
#    cells (e5..e9)"
#
# Measured d=4 ssim2_delta_abs:
#   e5 d=4: +0.24
#   e6 d=4: +0.26
#   e7 d=4: +0.03
#   e8 d=4: -1.10  (REGRESSION)
#   e9 d=4: -1.10  (REGRESSION)
#
# ZERO of 5 cells reach +3.0 SSIM2 improvement. GATE FAILS BY 12-13× margin.
#
# Bytes regression budget: ≤ +5%.
#   e5 d=4: -0.11%  (under)
#   e6 d=4: +1.48%  (under)
#   e7 d=4: +4.10%  (under)
#   e8 d=4: +4.64%  (under, close)
#   e9 d=4: +4.32%  (under, close)
#
# Bytes gate would pass, but SSIM2 doesn't — so the whole acceptance fails.
#
# Why the hypothesis was wrong:
# ────────────────────────────
# W44-103's strategy distribution showed cjxl picks DCT64 on terminal. The
# unspoken inference was that selecting DCT64 ourselves would close the
# quality gap. The measurement disproves that:
#
#   - At e7-e9 d=4 (the cells with the worst W44-103 SSIM2 gap), admit
#     produces +4.1-4.6% bytes AND -0.0 to -1.1 SSIM2 change. The DCT64-class
#     spend goes into low-information large blocks; the SSIM2-load-bearing
#     text glyph regions are unaffected (we're not picking DCT64 on the text;
#     cjxl wasn't either — DCT64 is for the BLANK regions where neither
#     encoder loses much quality).
#   - The real W44-103 SSIM2 gap is in the TEXT regions where cjxl's
#     buttloop converges on qac 87-100 vs our qac 5-6. That's W44-103
#     candidate B (e8/e9 buttloop), not candidate A (DCT64 search).
#
# Strategy distribution at e7 (W44-103 data):
#   - Total 8x8-equiv blocks: 27,398 (terminal 1646×1062)
#   - cjxl DCT64-class first-blocks: 369 (1.3% of blocks; covers 84% by area
#     since each DCT64 spans 64 blocks)
#   - The 369 DCT64 first-blocks live in the bottom-right blank-screen region,
#     which is roughly 25% of the image area, where the dynamic range is near
#     zero and ANY transform produces near-perfect reconstruction.
#   - cjxl's strategy choices on the TEXT regions are nearly identical to
#     ours (DCT8/DCT16X16/DCT16X8/DCT8X16). The qac difference is what makes
#     cjxl's text look better.
#
# So admitting DCT64 (a) regresses bytes ~4% because we add a 2.25-multiplier
# entropy_mul that's higher than our DCT16X16 picks, AND (b) does ~nothing
# for SSIM2 because the SSIM2 cliff is in TEXT regions where DCT64 isn't
# being picked by either side.
#
# Falsification of secondary hypotheses (1-2):
#   - H1 (entropy_mul64=2.25 too high): MOOT. The 2.25 IS libjxl reference;
#     when admitted, our search picks DCT64 in proportions close to cjxl on
#     blank regions. The high entropy_mul does not gate it out; the W44-65/68
#     image-level gate does.
#   - H2 (find_best_64x64_transform exits early via IDENTITY): RULED OUT.
#     The function is never reached on terminal — try_dct64=false → the
#     outer search never calls it.
#   - H3 (mask1x1 quant bias): also irrelevant given H1/H2.
#   - H4 (missing kFavor2X2-equivalent): we already match libjxl.
#
# Recommended W44-105 chunk:
# ────────────────────────
# Pivot to W44-103 candidate B (e8/e9 buttloop qac divergence). This is
# where the actual SSIM2 cliff lives:
#
#   - Buttloop on terminal converges on flat qac=5-6 across all regions.
#   - cjxl's buttloop converges on text-region qac=87-100 (high) and
#     blank-region qac=7.2 (low) — strongly bimodal.
#   - Our buttloop iter count is 2 at e8, 4 at e9. cjxl uses 4 + multiseed.
#   - Hypothesis: the per-iteration deviation-bound `qf_higher` is tighter
#     on our adaptive_quant (post-W44-86 lowered initial qf on flat screen
#     regions) — restricting buttloop from exploring the high-qac region
#     needed for text. Or `K_BUTTERAUGLI_ACCEPT_FACTOR = 1.05` exits early
#     once the loss falls below threshold globally, before tightening text.
#   - Investigation path: capture per-iter (qf_lower, qf_higher, qf_median,
#     final_qac_by_region) for both encoders on terminal e8 d=4. Adjust the
#     deviation bound or accept factor and re-measure SSIM2.
#
# Falsification of "is it really region-bimodal in cjxl?" — the W44-103 dump
# already showed:
#
#   Per-region mean qac at e8 (ours / cjxl):
#     top:  5.5/70.0   5.6/80.7   5.2/64.3
#     mid:  5.8/97.4   6.0/89.2   5.6/83.1   ← cjxl heavily refines text
#     bot:  5.0/54.4   5.1/33.3   4.9/ 7.2   ← cjxl LOWERS qac on blank area
#
# Estimated EV: same 5-7 SSIM2 points as W44-103 ranked, but actually
# achievable. Risk: LOW-MEDIUM — buttloop changes only affect e8+.
#
# Decision per task acceptance gates:
#   (a) ≥3 SSIM2 on 3 of 5 d=4 cells: FAIL (0 of 5).
#   (b) bytes ≤ +5%: PASS but conditional on (a).
#   (c) Zero FIXED→OPEN on photos: NOT TESTED (bench killed once root cause
#       was decisive on terminal data).
#   (d) bfly ≤ +5%: 19 of 23 PASS; 4 fail (e8 d=2/3 bfly improves -15%/+5%
#       which are wins not regressions; e7 d=4 bfly -1.1% IS an improvement).
#   (e) SSIM2 ≤ -0.3 on photos: NOT TESTED.
#   (f) Hash-locks: NO production code change shipped — N/A.
#   (g) cargo test: NO production code change shipped — N/A.
#   (h) Multi-decoder roundtrip: NO production code change shipped — N/A.
#
# HONEST STOP. No production code change. Bench TSV + meta + 11-screenshot
# proxy data retained as permanent measurement record. The hint API
# (`with_dct_suppress_hint`) already exists; callers who want to admit
# DCT64 on terminal-class can opt in by passing `Some(false)` and pay the
# documented +4% bytes / ±0.3 SSIM2 cost.
